A bigger memory-layout idea: for `B=1`, the triangular `bmm` output can be written into `[N, N, H]` interleaved storage via an `as_strided` view. That makes the output LayerNorm load contiguous hidden vectors instead of striding by `N*N`. I’ll test whether `torch.bmm` accepts that strided output and whether the faster output kernel offsets the write cost.
